u shalt put the testimony that I shall give thee.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙñAnd there I will meet with thee, and I will commune with thee from above the mercy seat, from between the two cherubims which are upon the ark of the testimony, of all things which I will give thee in commandment unto the children of Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses˜„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¡Thou shalt also make a table of shittim wood: two cubits shall be the length thereof, and a cubit the breadth thereof, and a cubit and a half the height thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWAnd thou shalt overlay it with pure gold, and make thereto a crown of gold round about.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŠAnd thou shalt make unto it a border of an hand breadth round about, and thou shalt make a golden crown to the border thereof round about.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd thou shalt make for it four rings of gold, and put the rings in the four corners that are on the four feet thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙVOver against the border shall the rings be for places of the staves to bear the table.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrAnd thou shalt make the staves of shittim wood, and overlay them with gold, that the table may be borne with them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–And thou shalt make the dishes thereof, and spoons thereof, and covers thereof, and bowls thereof, to cover withal: of pure gold shalt thou make them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<And thou shalt set upon the table shewbread before me alway.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse(¦versesš„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·And thou shalt make a candlestick of pure gold: of beaten work shall the candlestick be made: his shaft, and his branches, his bowls, his knops, and his flowers, shall be of the same.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ§And six branches shall come out of the sides of it; three branches of the candlestick out of the one side, and three branches of the candlestick out of the other side:¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÕthree bowls made like unto almonds, with a knop and a flower in one branch; and three bowls made like almonds in the other branch, with a knop and a flower: so in the six branches that come out of the candlestick.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙfAnd in the candlestick shall be four bowls made like unto almonds, with their knops and their flowers.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÒAnd there shall be a knop under two branches of the same, and a knop under two branches of the same, and a knop under two branches of the same, according to the six branches that proceed out of the candlestick.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbTheir knops and their branches shall be of the same: all it shall be one beaten work of pure gold.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ~And thou shalt make the seven lamps thereof: and they shall light the lamps thereof, that they may give light over against it.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJAnd the tongs thereof, and the snuffdishes thereof, shall be of pure gold.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBOf a talent of pure gold shall he make it, with all these vessels.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙUAnd look that thou make them after their pattern, which was shewed thee in the mount.¦layout ªlast_verse(